id=nemu_boot_autostart
name=Nemu Boot Guard
version=1.27
versionCode=28
author=Nemu
description=Auto-unbrick guard (3 failed boots): a verified clean shutdown or a user-requested root-side planned shutdown is not counted as a failed boot; watchdog/thermal reboots still count. v1.18 restores every Nemu-owned freeze state -- disable-user, hidden (pseudo-uninstall), suspend, disabled components, AppOps and standby buckets -- as soon as PackageManager answers at the early service stage (best-effort before the launcher), then verifies again after boot_completed; this covers unclean adb reboot/power loss and a frozen system app keeping the device on the boot screen. Normal/early passes are ownership-marker scoped; automatic rescue additionally restores Nemu's known target list but never scans arbitrary foreign suspensions. v1.19 sends the post-boot Nemu trigger with --include-stopped-packages and retries it, so a force-stopped or OEM-background-cleaned app still schedules the boot-freeze plan. v1.20 adds the deep-uninstall boot bridge: restore packages from /data/adb/nemu/deep_uninstall/manifest.tsv as soon as PackageManager answers, then re-uninstall only those restored this boot after boot_completed plus a 90 s stabilisation window; packages already installed at boot are never touched. v1.21 keeps app data on deep uninstall (pm uninstall -k --user 0), enables every restored package, records manifest.boot.tsv/manifest.last.tsv as a last-good boot baseline, adds deep_rescue.sh as an ABX package-restrictions last-resort rescue after a failed boot (only manifest packages; rolls back newly added entries so they are not re-uninstalled), and restores deep-uninstalled packages synchronously when the module is uninstalled. v1.22 fixes deep restore on MagicOS 10: pm has no install-multiple, and system_server cannot read the adb_data_file backups under /data/adb, so APKs are staged readably under /data/local/tmp and installed with pm install -r -d --user 0. v1.23 feeds every pm invocation /dev/null on stdin: cmd passes its stdin fd through binder, and a manifest file under /data/adb made every pm call die with Failed transaction (2147483646). v1.24 stores backup APKs as *.apk.bak (so system cleaners/scanners leave them alone) and renames them back to *.apk only in the /data/local/tmp staging directory before pm install; legacy *.apk backups still restore. v1.25 waits for a successful install-existing to appear in pm list before falling back; reinstalling during that commit window crashed MagicOS 10's PackageManager (removePackageLI NPE). v1.26 makes install-existing success authoritative: once it exits 0 the backup is never installed (the pm-list poll is only for logging), retries install-existing once on transient failures, and never falls back on "doesn't exist"/NameNotFoundException alone. v1.27 also refuses to install a backup when `pm list packages -u` still shows a system record (MagicOS delapp preloads): installing over that record crashes PackageManager; such apps come back on the next boot rescan.
